ad Tab — Product Spec## OverviewRedesign of the club admin's Squad tab in Talent Graph, replacing a flat mixed list of staff and players with a structured, scalable view built around how clubs actually organize their rosters.## Top-level structure- Two segments: **Players** and **Staff**, toggled via a segmented control at the top of the tab.- A search bar filters within whichever segment is active.- Header shows total counts: players, staff, and number of teams.---## Players### Team tiers- Players are grouped first by **team tier** — e.g. First XI/Team A, Team B, Academy.- Team tiers are **club-configurable**: not every club has all three, and clubs can add or remove tiers.- **Add Team**: quick-add available directly in the Squad tab (name only); full tier management (rename, delete, reorder) lives in club settings.- **Removing a tier** must prompt the admin to reassign its players to another tier first — a tier can never be deleted while it still holds players.- Each tier renders as a collapsible card (collapsed by default, except the first).### Position groups- Within each tier, players are grouped by position: Goalkeeper, Defence, Midfield, Wingers, Forwards, Strikers.- **Every position group always renders**, even with zero players, each with its own "Add Player" affordance — a section is an invitation to fill it, not something that only appears once populated.### Player row- Avatar/photo, name, verified badge (if applicable), age, and a **CSI score shown as a ring badge** (not a plain number) next to the photo.- A status dot (fit / knock / out) on the avatar corner.- A checkbox for multi-select.- An overflow menu (•••) per player with:  - View & edit details  - Transfer position  - Message player  - Delete player### Transfer- "Transfer position" moves a player **between positions within the same team tier** (e.g. Forward → Wingers) — it is not a cross-team transfer.- Triggered either per-player (overflow menu) or in bulk (see below). Presented as a bottom-sheet: pick the target position, confirm.### Bulk actions- Selecting one or more players (via checkboxes) surfaces a sticky action bar: **Transfer, Message, Delete**.- Bulk transfer assumes the selection is within a single position group.### Lineups (pitch view)- A global **"Lineups"** button opens a team picker (choose from the club's configured tiers).- Selecting a team opens a full-screen pitch/formation view: players are arranged in rows by position (GK → Defence → Midfield → Wingers → Forwards → Strikers), each showing photo, name, and **CSI score** (standing in for a match rating, since this is a squad-depth view, not a live-match lineup).- Empty tiers show an honest empty state rather than a broken/empty pitch.---## Staff### List- Flat list (no team-tier grouping needed for staff): avatar, name, role tag, message action, view-profile action.- **Add Staff**: a bottom-sheet form capturing name and role.### Org structure- An **"Org structure"** button opens a full-screen hierarchy view.- Staff are auto-sorted into three fixed tiers by role keyword:  1. **Head Coach** (head coach, manager)  2. **Assistant Coaches** (assistant coach, GK coach, fitness coach)  3. **Specialists & Scouts** (scout, physio, analyst, doctor, nutritionist)- Any role that doesn't match a keyword falls into an **"Other Staff"** tier so no one is silently dropped.- **Open question**: keyword-matching is a reasonable default, but a more robust version would let the admin explicitly assign a tier when adding a staff member (dropdown) rather than inferring it from free text — worth deciding before building for real.---## Visual language- Dark, data-terminal aesthetic (near-black background, signal-green accent for verified/positive states, monospace for numeric data like CSI) — consistent with Talent Graph's "Bloomberg Terminal for African football" positioning.- CSI shown as a radial ring badge wherever a player is displayed (list, pitch, etc.) rather than plain text, for faster scanning.## Reference artifacts- `squad-tab-v3.jsx` — current full implementation of the above (mock data, no backend wiring).
